# REVIEWABLE TEMPLATE -- not applied automatically. Validate with
# `visudo -cf` before installing, then copy to
# /etc/sudoers.d/rusty-fedora-agent (root-owned, mode 0440):
#
#   visudo -cf deploy/sudoers.d/rusty-fedora-agent
#   sudo install -o root -g root -m 0440 deploy/sudoers.d/rusty-fedora-agent \
#     /etc/sudoers.d/rusty-fedora-agent
#
# Scope is exactly `dnf install` and `dnf remove` with no further
# arguments constrained by sudoers itself -- the package-name allowlist
# (deploy/allowlist.toml's `packages` list) is enforced INSIDE the agent,
# before a `dnf` command is ever built, not by sudoers. This entry only
# answers "may rusty-fedora-agent run dnf install/remove as root at all,
# without a password" -- it does not and cannot know which package names
# are legitimate.
#
# Deliberately NOT `ALL` or a wildcard covering other dnf subcommands
# (upgrade, remove --all, reinstall, ...) -- widen this line only if a
# named tool needs it, matching README.md's "not included" list.

rusty-fedora-agent ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/dnf install *, /usr/bin/dnf remove *
